WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.537 --> 00:00:19.739
One beautiful October morning, Marilla and Anne sat in the kitchen and cut vegetables.

2
00:00:19.759 --> 00:00:26.122
"Anne," Marilla began, "why don't you ask Diana to come over for afternoon tea?

3
00:00:26.782 --> 00:00:29.203
I am going into town, and she can come then."

4
00:00:29.223 --> 00:00:31.104
"Oh, Marilla!"

5
00:00:31.504 --> 00:00:32.645
Anne clasped her hands.

6
00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.026
"How perfectly lovely!

7
00:00:35.546 --> 00:00:37.006
We will be like grown-ups!

8
00:00:37.607 --> 00:00:40.088
Can we use the teapot with the roses?"

9
00:00:40.108 --> 00:00:46.410
"No, but I have some cake and raspberry cordial in the pantry you can have," Marilla replied.

10
00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.772
Diana came over, dressed in her second-best dress.

11
00:00:51.632 --> 00:00:57.074
Anne, dressed in her own second-best dress, opened the door with a very serious expression.

12
00:00:57.775 --> 00:00:59.515
Together they went to the front room.

13
00:00:59.535 --> 00:01:01.096
"How is your mother?"

14
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.402
Anne asked politely, like an adult.

15
00:01:03.422 --> 00:01:05.623
"She is very well, thank you.

16
00:01:06.143 --> 00:01:06.624
And Mr.

17
00:01:06.684 --> 00:01:08.485
Cuthbert is in the potato fields?"

18
00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:09.666
asked Diana.

19
00:01:09.686 --> 00:01:11.747
"Yes, he is.

20
00:01:12.288 --> 00:01:15.570
Our potatoes are very good this year," replied Anne.

21
00:01:16.511 --> 00:01:18.132
Abruptly her tone changed.

22
00:01:18.152 --> 00:01:19.653
"Oh Diana!"

23
00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:20.854
she burst out.

24
00:01:20.874 --> 00:01:23.095
"Let's go and pick some apples!"

25
00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:29.320
The girls instantly stopped acting like proper ladies and ran outside to the apple orchard.

26
00:01:30.064 --> 00:01:33.586
"Marilla said we can pick the rest of the apples," said Anne.

27
00:01:33.966 --> 00:01:35.746
"Marilla is very kind.

28
00:01:36.387 --> 00:01:40.188
She also said we can have cake and raspberry cordial for tea.

29
00:01:40.748 --> 00:01:44.250
I love red drinks—they just taste better, don't they?"

30
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:50.632
Later the girls went inside, and Anne went to the pantry to get the raspberry cordial.

31
00:01:51.293 --> 00:01:55.214
At first she couldn't see it anywhere, but then she spotted it at the back.

32
00:01:56.295 --> 00:01:58.976
Anne put the cordial on the table with a big glass.

33
00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.301
"Please help yourself, Diana.

34
00:02:01.841 --> 00:02:04.523
I can't drink a thing after eating all those apples."

35
00:02:05.143 --> 00:02:07.904
Diana poured herself some of the drink and sipped it.

36
00:02:07.924 --> 00:02:11.806
"This is a very nice cordial, Anne," she said.

37
00:02:11.826 --> 00:02:14.488
"I didn't know cordial tasted so good."

38
00:02:14.508 --> 00:02:17.789
"I'm glad you like it," Anne replied.

39
00:02:17.809 --> 00:02:19.750
"Take as much as you want.

40
00:02:20.351 --> 00:02:21.171
I'll get the cake."

41
00:02:21.831 --> 00:02:25.865
When Anne came back, Diana was drinking a second glass of cordial.

42
00:02:26.365 --> 00:02:29.746
Diana started to drink a third glass, and Anne didn't mind.

43
00:02:29.766 --> 00:02:33.867
"It's the nicest cordial I ever drank," said Diana.

44
00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:36.148
"It's much nicer than Mrs.

45
00:02:36.228 --> 00:02:37.128
Lynde's cordial.

46
00:02:37.708 --> 00:02:39.849
It doesn't taste a bit like hers."

47
00:02:39.869 --> 00:02:43.210
"I'm sure Marilla's cordial is nicer than Mrs.

48
00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.370
Lynde's," said Anne loyally.

49
00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.791
"Marilla is a famous cook.

50
00:02:48.491 --> 00:02:51.872
She's trying to teach me, but it's hard work, Diana.

51
00:02:52.648 --> 00:02:58.690
Last week," Anne continued, "Marilla told me to put some pudding sauce in the pantry and cover it.

52
00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:03.351
I took the bowl of sauce into the pantry, but I forgot to cover it.

53
00:03:03.932 --> 00:03:06.652
I remembered the next morning and ran to the pantry.

54
00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:10.694
Diana, a mouse had drowned in the sauce!

55
00:03:11.374 --> 00:03:14.235
I used a spoon to get the mouse and took it outside.

56
00:03:14.815 --> 00:03:17.596
Then I was going to tell Marilla about the mouse.

57
00:03:18.456 --> 00:03:23.998
But I started pretending I was a forest fairy flying through the trees, and I forgot about the

58
00:03:24.038 --> 00:03:25.498
mouse and the sauce.

59
00:03:26.218 --> 00:03:27.579
After that Mr.

60
00:03:27.619 --> 00:03:28.059
and Mrs.

61
00:03:28.139 --> 00:03:29.339
Ross came for lunch.

62
00:03:29.879 --> 00:03:35.861
We ate lunch and everything was fine until I saw Marilla coming in with plum pudding and pudding

63
00:03:36.001 --> 00:03:37.281
sauce, warmed up.

64
00:03:38.001 --> 00:03:42.063
I remembered everything and shouted, 'Marilla, don't use the sauce.

65
00:03:42.723 --> 00:03:44.183
A mouse drowned in it!'

66
00:03:44.903 --> 00:03:45.704
Mr. and Mrs.

67
00:03:45.764 --> 00:03:49.129
Ross looked at me, and I thought I would die!

68
00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.551
Why, Diana," Anne said suddenly.

69
00:03:52.571 --> 00:03:54.092
"What's the matter?"

70
00:03:55.693 --> 00:03:59.915
Diana stood up and then sat down, putting her hands to her head.

71
00:03:59.935 --> 00:04:03.517
"I'm I'm very sick," she said.

72
00:04:03.537 --> 00:04:06.779
"I I must go home."

73
00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:08.920
"No, don't go yet.

74
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.381
You must eat some cake first."

75
00:04:11.401 --> 00:04:14.543
"I must go home," Diana repeated.

76
00:04:14.563 --> 00:04:16.484
"Where do you feel bad?"

77
00:04:16.848 --> 00:04:17.449
Anne asked.

78
00:04:17.989 --> 00:04:20.871
"I'm very dizzy," said Diana.

79
00:04:21.511 --> 00:04:25.553
Anne was very disappointed, but she took Diana to the Barrys' fence.

80
00:04:26.674 --> 00:04:29.376
The next day Marilla sent Anne to Mrs.

81
00:04:29.456 --> 00:04:30.797
Lynde's house on an errand.

82
00:04:31.417 --> 00:04:36.280
In a short space of time, Anne came flying back to Green Gables in tears.

83
00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.221
"What's the matter, Anne?"

84
00:04:38.681 --> 00:04:39.382
Marilla said.

85
00:04:39.402 --> 00:04:42.924
"Mrs. Lynde saw Diana's mother today.

86
00:04:43.576 --> 00:04:46.978
Mrs. Barry said that I sent Diana home drunk.

87
00:04:47.638 --> 00:04:53.961
And she said I was a very wicked girl and she's never, never going to let Diana play

88
00:04:53.981 --> 00:04:55.101
with me again!"

89
00:04:55.121 --> 00:04:57.862
"Diana was drunk?"

90
00:04:58.343 --> 00:04:59.503
Marilla was stunned.

91
00:04:59.523 --> 00:05:01.884
"Anne, are you or Mrs.

92
00:05:01.944 --> 00:05:02.884
Barry crazy?

93
00:05:03.605 --> 00:05:04.665
What did you give her?"

94
00:05:04.685 --> 00:05:08.247
"Nothing but raspberry cordial," Anne said.

95
00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:14.381
"I never thought it made you drunk, not even if you drink three glasses like Diana did."

96
00:05:15.021 --> 00:05:16.642
Marilla marched to the pantry.

97
00:05:17.262 --> 00:05:19.902
On the shelf was a bottle of homemade wine.

98
00:05:20.643 --> 00:05:26.644
At that moment Marilla remembered that the cordial was in the cellar and not the pantry as she

99
00:05:26.684 --> 00:05:27.485
had told Anne.

100
00:05:28.525 --> 00:05:30.165
Marilla went back into the kitchen.

101
00:05:30.185 --> 00:05:34.206
"Anne, you gave Diana wine instead of cordial!

102
00:05:34.727 --> 00:05:36.487
Don't you know the difference between them?"

103
00:05:36.507 --> 00:05:39.848
"I didn't taste the drink," said Anne.

104
00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.121
"Only Diana drank it.

105
00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:45.824
And then Diana got so sick and went home.

106
00:05:46.564 --> 00:05:53.609
Mrs. Barry said Diana just laughed and laughed, and then slept for hours, and had a headache all

107
00:05:53.669 --> 00:05:57.672
day. Her mother smelled her breath and knew she was drunk."

108
00:05:58.912 --> 00:06:03.235
"Three glasses of cordial would make you sick," Marilla said, troubled.

109
00:06:03.255 --> 00:06:06.177
"But it was an accident, Anne, so don't worry.

110
00:06:06.818 --> 00:06:07.658
I'll talk to Mrs.

111
00:06:07.718 --> 00:06:09.960
Barry." At that, Marilla left.

112
00:06:10.652 --> 00:06:12.833
When she came back later, she was frowning.

113
00:06:12.853 --> 00:06:14.253
"Was Mrs.

114
00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:15.833
Barry still angry?"

115
00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:16.794
asked Anne.

116
00:06:16.814 --> 00:06:18.534
"Mrs. Barry?"

117
00:06:19.014 --> 00:06:19.835
snapped Marilla.

118
00:06:19.855 --> 00:06:23.956
"I told her it was a mistake, but she didn't believe me.

119
00:06:24.596 --> 00:06:30.957
So I told her that if my girl was so greedy, drinking three glasses of anything, I'd be

120
00:06:30.997 --> 00:06:31.898
punishing her!"

121
00:06:33.238 --> 00:06:34.618
Marilla went into the kitchen.

122
00:06:35.259 --> 00:06:40.160
Anne stepped outside, and she walked determinedly to the Barrys' house and knocked on the door.

123
00:06:40.852 --> 00:06:41.392
When Mrs.

124
00:06:41.452 --> 00:06:43.554
Barry saw it was Anne, she frowned.

125
00:06:44.374 --> 00:06:45.835
"What do you want?"

126
00:06:46.395 --> 00:06:47.136
she demanded.

127
00:06:47.836 --> 00:06:49.137
Anne clasped her hands.

128
00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:50.678
"Oh, Mrs.

129
00:06:50.778 --> 00:06:52.719
Barry, please forgive me.

130
00:06:52.739 --> 00:06:57.842
I did not mean to to make Diana drunk.

131
00:06:58.542 --> 00:06:59.323
How could I?

132
00:06:59.903 --> 00:07:02.265
She is my best friend in the world.

133
00:07:02.885 --> 00:07:04.726
I thought it was raspberry cordial.

134
00:07:05.346 --> 00:07:07.808
Please say that you'll let me play with Diana.

135
00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:15.063
If I can't play with her, my life will be covered by a huge dark cloud of sadness."

136
00:07:15.903 --> 00:07:18.564
Anne's dramatic plea had no effect on Mrs.

137
00:07:18.644 --> 00:07:23.146
Barry. She said coldly, "Anne, you should go home.

138
00:07:23.706 --> 00:07:26.267
You are not a good friend for Diana."

139
00:07:26.287 --> 00:07:31.489
"Can't I see Diana and just say one last good-bye?"

140
00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:32.510
Anne asked.

141
00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:36.031
"Diana is out with her father," said Mrs.

142
00:07:36.091 --> 00:07:37.372
Barry, shutting the door.

143
00:07:38.212 --> 00:07:40.873
Anne walked back to Green Gables with her head down.

144
00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:46.435
"My last hope is gone," she told Marilla, full of despair.

145
00:07:46.455 --> 00:07:48.275
"I talked to Mrs.

146
00:07:48.375 --> 00:07:51.376
Barry, and she treated me very badly.

147
00:07:51.396 --> 00:07:54.377
I can do nothing now but pray.

148
00:07:54.917 --> 00:07:59.438
But I don't think that will help because even God can't change Mrs.

149
00:07:59.539 --> 00:08:00.459
Barry's mind."

150
00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:07.913
"Anne, don't talk like that," said Marilla, trying not to laugh at Anne's theatrics.

151
00:08:08.734 --> 00:08:15.024
But later Marilla couldn't help feeling pity for Anne when she saw that the child had cried herself

152
00:08:15.084 --> 00:08:15.604
to sleep.

153
00:08:15.624 --> 00:08:20.392
"Poor little thing," Marilla whispered, kissing Anne's red cheek.
